A||||1||FieroPerformance||New engine break-in procedures?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||11-24-2001||06:15 PM||||I just got done rebuilding my 2.8. It is all new on the inside except for heads, block, crank, and connecting rods. I have a compucam performance cam and power forged pistons. I was wondering if there are any special things I should be doing to break it in other than taking it easy and keeping it under 55, and varying the speed. How many miles do I have to take it easy? I am dieing to wind it up and see how fast it is.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||11-24-2001||06:24 PM||||Drive moderately, no faster than 80kph for extended periods, no revving, no lugging. Do this for 1000km (so I'm told).<P>After that, Change oil/filter and drive normally. Don't baby it, and don't flog it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
